    "title": "Andrew Clyde posts about gender identity and Somali TPS on social media",
    "text": "Rep. Andrew Clyde, a member of the U.S. House of Representatives, posted a series of tweets on January 13 and 14, 2026, addressing issues related to gender identity and immigration policy.\nOn January 13, Clyde wrote: “TWO sexes. ONE truth. ZERO men in women’s sports.” (January 13, 2026). The tweet appears to reference ongoing debates over transgender participation in women’s sports.\nThe following day, Clyde commented on recent federal immigration policy changes: “The Trump Administration just ENDED Temporary Protected Status for Somalis in the United States. They must LEAVE America by March 17—or face DEPORTATION. Thank you, President Trump, for delivering America First accountability!” (January 14, 2026).\nLater that same day, Clyde addressed Delaware State Senator Sarah McBride with another post: “Tim ‘Sarah’ McBride is a man. No amount of makeup can change this biological truth.” (January 14, 2026).\nAndrew Clyde has been elected multiple times to Congress from Georgia’s Ninth District. He won his most recent election in 2024 against Tambrei Cash with nearly seventy percent of the vote and had similar margins in previous elections against Michael Ford in 2022 and Devin Pandy in 2020.",
